Chapter: CityKeeperLeisure
  cites Uoaix chapter CityWorkers
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGatherer
  cites Uoaix chapter BritainShopHours
  cites Uoaix chapter KeeperLeisure
  cites Uoaix chapter TownLivePath
  cites Uoaix chapter Teleporters

  CkKeeper = record { vendor : Integer, payee : Integer, box : BbShop, inn : BbShop, town : TownLive, map : WalkMap,
    work : BbSpot, out : BbSpot, walk : RteWalk, next-step : Integer, goal : Integer, paid : Integer, seen : Integer, stop : Integer, refused : Integer, refused-2 : Integer, via : Integer }
 A city keeper is out on two nights in three, as a worker is (cgg-out-on).
  ck-out-on : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  ck-out-on (vendor) (night) = int-mod (vendor + night) 3 /= 0
  ck-goal : Integer, Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  ck-goal (vendor) (shut) (now) = let hour = int-mod (now / 3600) 24
    in if shut & hour >= bsh-close-hour & hour < bsh-tavern-hour & ck-out-on vendor (bsh-night now) then 2 else 1
  ck-role-vendor : CgCity, Integer -> Integer
  ck-role-vendor (c) (role) = if role < 0 | role >= list-length c.vendors then -1 else list-at c.vendors role
 A keeper's evening is personal spending (root for Damian, 2026-10-13): it is paid from the keeper's own wage purse
 (UOAIX-239, kind 2, owner ck-wage-base + vendor index), and a keeper whose purse cannot pay a drink stays at the shop.
  ck-wage-base : Integer = 4000
  ck-wallet : GvWorld, Integer -> Integer
  ck-wallet (v) (vendor) = em-find v.currency.world.money 2 (ck-wage-base + vendor) 1
  ck-can-pay : EuCurrency, Integer -> Boolean
  ck-can-pay (x) (purse) = if purse < 1 | purse > x.world.money.purse-count then False
    else (em-purse x.copper purse).coin >= kl-drink-price | (em-purse x.silver purse).coin >= 1 | (em-purse x.world.money purse).coin >= 1
  ck-payee : CgCity -> Integer
  ck-payee (c) = if ck-role-vendor c bb-tavern-keeper >= 0 then ck-role-vendor c bb-tavern-keeper else ck-role-vendor c bb-inn
  ck-spot : Integer -> BbSpot
  ck-spot (unused) = BbSpot { x = 0, y = 0, z = 0 }
 cgs and towns are cw-build's parallel lists, Britain first: a city's town is at the city's own index. Indexing a list
 with Britain removed gave each city the town before it, whose planner is another map's size, so every plan failed
 (trial 44288: due 66 to 69 a night, can-pay all of them, arrived 0).
  ck-town-index : List CgCity, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-town-index (cgs) (city) (i) = if i >= list-length cgs | city == 0 then 0 - 1
    else if (list-at cgs i).city == city then i else ck-town-index cgs city (i + 1)
  ck-build : GvWorld, List BbShop, List CtCity, List CgCity, List TownLive, List WalkMap, Integer, List CkKeeper -> List CkKeeper
  ck-build (v) (shops) (cities) (cgs) (towns) (maps) (k) (out) = if k >= v.vendor-count | k - bb-shop-count >= list-length shops then out
    else let box = list-at shops (k - bb-shop-count)
    in let city = ct-city-at cities box.x1 box.y1 0
    in let at = ck-town-index cgs city 0
    in if at < 0 | at >= list-length towns then ck-build v shops cities cgs towns maps (k + 1) out
    else let c = list-at cgs at
    in let payee = ck-payee c
    in if payee < 0 | payee == k then ck-build v shops cities cgs towns maps (k + 1) out
    else when ct-map-of maps city
      is None -> ck-build v shops cities cgs towns maps (k + 1) out
      is Just (map) -> ck-build v shops cities cgs towns maps (k + 1) (out & [CkKeeper { vendor = k, payee = payee, box = box, inn = c.inn, town = list-at towns at, map = map,
        work = ck-spot 0, out = ck-spot 0, walk = rte-walk 0, next-step = 0, goal = 0 - 1, paid = 0, seen = 0, stop = 0, refused = 0, refused-2 = 0, via = 0 - 1 }])
 Tally (ck-tally-bytes): 0 the night counted (night + 1), 8 keepers arrived, 16 paid, 56 keepers due out that evening,
 64 of those whose wage purse could pay a drink; 24, 32, 40, 72, 80 the last finished night's five; 48 the night last
 reported (night + 1). The night rolls on the first step of a new night, so a night no keeper reached still reports.
 88, 96, 104 the keepers whose evening ended unarrived: no tile at the inn, no route held, or still walking; 112, 120,
 128 the last finished night's three. 136 to 263 the first eight no-route keepers of the night, two qwords each
 (vendor * 16 + plan failures at most 15, then the keeper's last failed plan's stop, ck-stop-pack), 264 to 391 the
 last finished night's eight.
  ck-tally-bytes : Integer = 392
  ck-named : Integer = 8
  ck-named-at : Integer = 136
  ck-named-last : Integer = 264
  ck-copy-named : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-copy-named (tally) (i) = if i >= ck-named * 2 then 0
    else let moved = poke-qword tally (ck-named-last + i * 8) (peek-qword tally (ck-named-at + i * 8)) in let cleared = poke-qword tally (ck-named-at + i * 8) 0 in ck-copy-named tally (i + 1)
  ck-roll : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-roll (tally) (night) = if peek-qword tally 0 == night + 1 then 0
    else let a = poke-qword tally 24 (peek-qword tally 0) in let b = poke-qword tally 32 (peek-qword tally 8) in let c = poke-qword tally 40 (peek-qword tally 16)
    in let f = poke-qword tally 72 (peek-qword tally 56) in let g = poke-qword tally 80 (peek-qword tally 64)
    in let j = poke-qword tally 112 (peek-qword tally 88) in let k = poke-qword tally 120 (peek-qword tally 96) in let l = poke-qword tally 128 (peek-qword tally 104)
    in let p = ck-copy-named tally 0
    in let m = poke-qword tally 88 0 in let n = poke-qword tally 96 0 in let o = poke-qword tally 104 0
    in let d = poke-qword tally 0 (night + 1) in let e = poke-qword tally 8 0 in let h = poke-qword tally 56 0 in let i = poke-qword tally 64 0 in poke-qword tally 16 0
  ck-missed : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-missed (tally) (spot-x) (route) = let at = if spot-x == 0 then 88 else if route < 0 then 96 else 104
    in poke-qword tally at (peek-qword tally at + 1)
  ck-name-missed : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-name-missed (tally) (vendor) (fails) (stop) = let n = peek-qword tally 96 - 1
    in if n < 0 | n >= ck-named then 0
    else let named = poke-qword tally (ck-named-at + n * 16) (vendor * 16 + min 15 fails) in poke-qword tally (ck-named-at + n * 16 + 8) stop
 A stop packs the expanded tile nearest the goal, its distance in tiles (Chebyshev, at most 1023) and why the search
 ended (tl-ended-budget, tl-ended-sealed); 0 is a keeper with no failed search of its own.
  ck-stop-pack : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-stop-pack (x) (y) (d) (why) = ((x * 8192 + y) * 1024 + min 1023 d) * 4 + why
  ck-stop-text : Integer -> Text
  ck-stop-text (s) = if s == 0 then "@none"
    else "@" & show (s / 4 / 1024 / 8192) & "." & show (int-mod (s / 4 / 1024) 8192) & ".d" & show (int-mod (s / 4) 1024)
      & (if int-mod s 4 == tl-ended-budget then ".budget" else if int-mod s 4 == tl-ended-sealed then ".sealed" else ".other")
 A sealed search expanded every cell its start reaches, and a city map carries no doors, so the same start and target
 are never planned again by that keeper (root, 2026-10-16): the search runs inside the world tick and costs the whole
 region. A keeper keeps two refusals, the way out and the way back.
  ck-pair : WorldObject, BbSpot -> Integer
  ck-pair (from) (target) = bsh-pair from target
  ck-refusal : Integer, WorldObject, BbSpot -> Integer
  ck-refusal (ended) (from) (target) = if ended == tl-ended-sealed then ck-pair from target else 0
  ck-refuses : CkKeeper, Integer -> Boolean
  ck-refuses (k) (pair) = k.refused == pair | k.refused-2 == pair
  ck-note-stop : CkKeeper, WorldObject, BbSpot -> Integer
  ck-note-stop (k) (from) (target) = let p = k.town.nav
    in if p.near < 0 then 0
    else let s = __record-set k "stop" (ck-stop-pack (k.map.x + int-mod p.near p.width) (k.map.y + p.near / p.width) (p.near-h / tl-step-cost) p.ended)
    in ck-store k (ck-refusal p.ended from target)
  ck-store : CkKeeper, Integer -> Integer
  ck-store (k) (refusal) = if refusal == 0 then 0 else if k.refused == 0 then (let r = __record-set k "refused" refusal in 0) else (let r = __record-set k "refused-2" refusal in 0)
  ck-job-base : Integer = 1000
  ck-job-answer : Maybe RteJob, Integer -> Integer
  ck-job-answer (job) (who) = when job is None -> 0 is Just (j) -> rte-job-answer j who
  ck-ask : Maybe RteJob, Integer, CkKeeper, WorldObject, BbSpot -> Integer
  ck-ask (job) (who) (k) (npc) (aim) = when job
    is None -> 0
    is Just (j) -> if rte-job-ask j who k.town.nav k.map False npc aim.x aim.y aim.z then 1 else 0
 A keeper refused its target from where it stands walks to the teleporter in its city's window nearest it whose
 destination lies nearer the target, and is carried there on arrival (Jhelom's herbalist on the south island).
  ck-pick-via : Integer, WalkMap, WorldObject, BbSpot, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-pick-via (tp) (map) (npc) (target) (i) (best) (best-d) = cgg-pick-via tp map npc.x npc.y target i best best-d
  ck-carry : CkKeeper, GvWorld, WorldObject, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-carry (k) (v) (npc) (tp) (now) = let i = k.via
    in let moved = WorldObject { serial = npc.serial, kind = 1, x = tp-at tp i 3, y = tp-at tp i 4, z = tp-at tp i 5,
      graphic = npc.graphic, hue = npc.hue, container = 0, amount = 1, health = npc.health }
    in let cleared = __record-set k "via" (0 - 1)
    in let dropped = rte-drop k.walk
    in let next = __record-set k "next-step" (now + 1)
    in when world-update v.game.world moved is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (_) -> let touched = world-touch v.game.world in 0
  ck-count : Integer, Integer, Boolean -> Integer
  ck-count (tally) (night) (paid) = let rolled = ck-roll tally night
    in let out = poke-qword tally 8 (peek-qword tally 8 + 1)
    in if paid then poke-qword tally 16 (peek-qword tally 16 + 1) else 0
  ck-due : CkKeeper, Integer, Integer, Boolean -> Integer
  ck-due (k) (tally) (night) (funded) = if k.seen == night + 1 then 0
    else let marked = __record-set k "seen" (night + 1)
    in let due = poke-qword tally 56 (peek-qword tally 56 + 1)
    in if funded then poke-qword tally 64 (peek-qword tally 64 + 1) else 0
  ck-pay : CkKeeper, GvWorld, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-pay (k) (v) (tally) (now) = let night = bsh-night now
    in if k.paid == night + 1 | k.payee >= v.vendor-count then 0
    else let marked = __record-set k "paid" (night + 1)
    in let w = v.currency.world
    in let wallet = ck-wallet v k.vendor
    in let paid = wallet > 0 & kl-pay-coin v.currency wallet (ep-actor w (list-at v.vendors k.payee).actor).purse kl-drink-price == 0
    in let counted = ck-count tally night paid in if paid then 1 else 0
  ck-fix-work : CkKeeper, GvWorld, WorldObject -> Integer
  ck-fix-work (k) (v) (npc) = if bsh-inside k.box npc.x npc.y 0 then tl-copy-spot k.work (BbSpot { x = npc.x, y = npc.y, z = npc.z })
    else when bb-placement v.game.world k.map k.box 0 is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (spot) -> tl-copy-spot k.work spot
  ck-pick-out : CkKeeper, GvWorld -> Integer
  ck-pick-out (k) (v) = when bb-placement v.game.world k.map k.inn (ck-out-index k.vendor k.inn)
    is Ok (spot) -> tl-copy-spot k.out spot
    is Err (_) -> when bb-placement v.game.world k.map k.inn 0
      is Err (_) -> tl-copy-spot k.out (ck-spot 0)
      is Ok (spot) -> tl-copy-spot k.out spot
  ck-out-index : Integer, BbShop -> Integer
  ck-out-index (vendor) (inn) = int-mod vendor (max 1 ((inn.x2 - inn.x1 + 1) * (inn.y2 - inn.y1 + 1)))
  ck-settle : CkKeeper, Integer -> Integer
  ck-settle (k) (now) = let rest = __record-set k "next-step" (bsh-next-change now) in rte-drop k.walk
 A city keeper's plan expands at most rte-slice cells in its step; a longer one goes to the staff's RteJob (Nujel'm's
 west shops need 16802 cells to the inn and Vesper's Shimmering Jewel 32115).
 One step of keeper k; the answer is 1 when the step started a route plan.
  ck-step : CkKeeper, GvWorld, Integer, Maybe RteJob, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-step (k) (v) (tp) (job) (tally) (now) (left) = let wanted = ck-goal k.vendor (gv-shut v k.vendor) now
    in let funded = if wanted == 2 then ck-can-pay v.currency (ck-wallet v k.vendor) else False
    in let counted = if wanted == 2 then ck-due k tally (bsh-night now) funded else 0
    in let goal = if wanted == 2 & not funded then 1 else wanted
    in if k.next-step > now & k.goal == goal then 0
    else when world-get v.game.world (list-at v.vendors k.vendor).serial
      is Err (_) -> 0
      is Ok (npc) -> if npc.kind /= 1 | npc.health <= 0 then 0
        else let fixed = if k.work.x == 0 then ck-fix-work k v npc else 0
        in let missed = if k.goal == 2 & goal == 1 & k.paid /= bsh-night now + 1 then
            (let counted = ck-missed tally k.out.x k.walk.route in if k.out.x /= 0 & k.walk.route < 0 then ck-name-missed tally k.vendor k.walk.fails k.stop else 0)
          else 0
        in let changed = if k.goal == goal then 0
          else let selected = __record-set k "goal" goal in let dropped = rte-drop k.walk in let unvia = __record-set k "via" (0 - 1) in if goal == 2 then ck-pick-out k v else 0
        in let target = if k.goal == 2 then k.out else k.work
        in if target.x == 0 then (let settled = ck-settle k now in 0)
        else if (k.goal == 1 & bsh-inside k.box npc.x npc.y 0) | (k.goal == 2 & bsh-inside k.inn npc.x npc.y 0) | tl-at npc target then
          (let paid = if k.goal == 2 then ck-pay k v tally now else 0 in let settled = ck-settle k now in 0)
        else let plans = k.walk.route < 0
        in let picked = if plans & k.via < 0 & ck-refuses k (ck-pair npc target) then (let p = __record-set k "via" (ck-pick-via tp k.map npc target 0 (0 - 1) 0) in 0) else 0
        in if k.via >= 0 & npc.x == tp-at tp k.via 0 & npc.y == tp-at tp k.via 1 then ck-carry k v npc tp now
        else let aim = if k.via >= 0 then BbSpot { x = tp-at tp k.via 0, y = tp-at tp k.via 1, z = tp-at tp k.via 2 } else target
        in let who = ck-job-base + k.vendor
        in let answer = if plans then ck-job-answer job who else 0
        in let sealed = if answer == 3 then ck-store k (ck-pair npc aim) else 0
        in if answer == 1 then (let rest = __record-set k "next-step" (now + 1) in 0)
        else if plans & ck-refuses k (ck-pair npc aim) then (let rest = __record-set k "next-step" (now + tl-retry-seconds) in 0)
        else if plans & left <= 0 then 0
        else let rested = if answer == 2 then (let r = __record-set k.walk "rest" 0 in 0) else 0
        in let moves = k.walk.moves
        in let epoch = k.town.nav.epoch
        in when rte-toward-budget k.town.nav v.game.world (Just v.game) k.map None rte-any k.walk npc aim.x aim.y aim.z rte-slice
          is Err (_) -> let rest = __record-set k "next-step" (now + tl-retry-seconds) in 0
          is Ok (_) -> let failed = plans & k.walk.route < 0 & k.town.nav.epoch /= epoch
          in let stopped = if failed then ck-note-stop k npc aim else 0
          in let asked = if failed & k.town.nav.ended == tl-ended-budget then ck-ask job who k npc aim else 0
          in let queued = if failed & k.town.nav.ended == tl-ended-budget then rte-queued k.walk else 0
          in let next = __record-set k "next-step" (now + (if asked == 1 | k.walk.moves /= moves then 1 else tl-retry-seconds)) in if plans then 1 else 0
 At most bsh-plans keepers start a route plan in one step, as Britain's keepers do (UOAIX-216).
  ck-step-all : List CkKeeper, GvWorld, Integer, Maybe RteJob, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ck-step-all (keepers) (v) (tp) (job) (tally) (now) (i) (left) = if i >= list-length keepers then 0
    else let rolled = if i == 0 then ck-roll tally (bsh-night now) else 0
    in let used = ck-step (list-at keepers i) v tp job tally now left
    in used + ck-step-all keepers v tp job tally now (i + 1) (left - used)
